  "title": "Russian Empire",
  "summary": "In 1721 Peter the Great proclaimed Russia an empire and took the title of Emperor of All Russia. Saint Petersburg, begun under Peter in 1703, became the empire's capital. Serfdom lasted until 1861, when an emancipation manifesto freed about 23 million serfs. In the First World War its huge armies suffered enormous casualties. The February Revolution of 1917 forced Tsar Nicholas II to abdicate, ending three hundred years of Romanov rule.",
